diff --git a/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/CONTROL-SESSION.md b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/CONTROL-SESSION.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..09955f1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/CONTROL-SESSION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,92 @@
+# P4 offline control session
+
+`ControlSession` is a serialized scheduler over the P3 identity registry. It has
+no transport or device permission. `poll` returns at most two commands, one per
+connected slot; the caller validates the original command immediately before a
+mock dispatch and returns the exact result once. The P4 runtime owns the
+transport, message, thermal and final CAN-dispatch boundaries. This class alone
+is not a deployed daemon or MCU safety policy.
+
+## Barriers and state
+
+Both bound slots require a current exact 48-byte health packet and three current
+exact 64-byte CAN-health packets. Known wire enums/flags, F4 CAN-FD restrictions,
+no bus-off/error-warning/error-passive, and the noOutput health contract are
+checked before availability. Unknown/short data is not converted to healthy
+zeros. A malformed packet clears the corresponding old snapshot; a valid packet
+that reports a fault is retained as that actual fault snapshot. Whole-group
+publication and simulated CAN admission remain false on either outcome.
+
+Configuration accepts exactly two slot-ordered entries and only the pinned
+`noOutput` enum 19. Each slot has its own uint16 parameter and known
+alternative-experience bits (2|8|16), with no index-0 replication, implicit ELM327
+or allOutput. Every accepted configuration requires a caller-verified fresh
+offroad envelope, sends alternative experience then safety, and requires a
+post-write health readback of all three values. `controls_allowed` must be false
+for noOutput; it is not synthesized to make the simulated host gate pass.
+
+A complete readback group still cannot engage until a fresh disabled sample
+followed by a newer enabled sample is observed. Samples retain their source
+monotonic time and registry generation. Duplicates, invalid Events, future or
+expired timestamps close the group. Reconfiguration, lifecycle changes and
+faults erase the prior edge. A frozen enabled state cannot keep heartbeats
+engaged. After a fault, a fresh offroad configuration and new disabled/enabled
+edge are required; reconnect alone never rearms.
+
+`control_epoch` supplements the P3 registry generation. It changes on every
+registry-generation synchronization, fault, accepted reconfiguration and normal
+armed-to-disabled transition. The runtime captures both at message ingress and
+flushes/rejects old CAN batches/intents across either change. It is not a
+cryptographic capability. Public command fields are checked against the exact
+single pending command per slot before completion. Command IDs/control epochs
+never wrap; test-only seeds initialize an empty scheduler to exercise exhaustion.
+
+## Frozen candidate host budgets
+
+These are deterministic offline scheduling contracts, not measured device or
+kernel real-time guarantees. Health/heartbeat constants reuse P2 without changing
+its policy tests. P4 additionally rejects clock rollback/wrap permanently.
+
+| Item | Budget / boundary |
+| --- | --- |
+| Health and each CAN-health polling period | 100,000 us |
+| Health and CAN-health valid age | strictly below 250,000 us |
+| Heartbeat polling period | 100,000 us |
+| Successful heartbeat valid age | strictly below 250,000 us |
+| selfdrive source age | strictly below 100,000 us |
+| Pending command/completion age | strictly below 100,000 us |
+| Pending command capacity | one per slot; no backlog/retry queue |
+| Commands returned per poll | at most two, one per connected slot |
+| Initial configuration | nine poll rounds: exit safety, exit readback, disengaged heartbeat, alternative experience, safety, health, CAN-health 0/1/2 |
+| Fault exit | three poll rounds: noOutput(19,0), exact health readback, disengaged heartbeat |
+
+At the runtime's 10 ms cooperative tick bound, initial configuration needs at
+most 90 ms of scheduler rounds, and explicit fault exit needs at most 30 ms,
+provided each fake backend honors the finite call budget and the caller runs the
+loop. Health and heartbeat deadlines close the host gate at the next owner
+inspection. This does not promise preemption of a stalled kernel ioctl.
+
+An uncertain/failed command, expired pending operation, unexpected write reply
+or failed exit readback retires that slot's connection token. The same write is
+never retried, and its sibling receives its own explicit exit sequence. A
+surviving slot is never promoted or used to replay a rejected frame. Normal
+disengagement already has verified noOutput on both boards, retains that
+configuration and sends an immediate disengaged heartbeat; fault exit explicitly
+writes noOutput(19,0) and reads it back before the heartbeat.
+
+Historical nonzero TX-blocked, invalid-RX, overflow, SPI and CAN error counters
+are retained. Any subsequent delta, including reset/wrap, and decreasing uptime
+close the group instead of claiming a clean current session. Nonzero current
+fault/status, heartbeat lost, safety-RX invalid, reset or power-save flags also
+close the active simulation barrier. This conservative policy may require a
+fresh offline configuration even after an otherwise recoverable condition.
+
+## MCU distinction
+
+The separately compiled pinned firmware oracle proves that a disengaged
+heartbeat does not immediately force controls false: firmware uses three 1 Hz
+mismatch checks. Its heartbeat timeout independently enters SILENT at the pinned
+ignition-dependent counter thresholds, while the software-watchdog fault is a
+different path. The host exit sequence therefore does not rely on an immediate
+heartbeat side effect. No real MCU watchdog, power loss, C3XL fan behavior,
+vehicle safety or target deployment is validated by these host tests.
diff --git a/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/P4-INTEGRATION.md b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/P4-INTEGRATION.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..354180e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/P4-INTEGRATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,110 @@
+# P4: explicit pandad offline integration
+
+The locked official default remains the single-SPI device path. The same Linux
+`pandad` executable now has an explicit `--compat-offline` entry dispatched before
+logging, priority setup or hardware discovery. It runs bounded synthetic fixtures
+through the shared `PandadRuntime`, P2 Transport over in-memory fake Backends,
+P3 routing, the P4 control session and the unchanged cereal wire schema. It exits;
+it does not subscribe to live messaging or construct physical Panda/USB handles.
+This is an offline integration build, not an installation or vehicle runtime.
+
+The Python wrapper dispatches the same explicit entry before importing Panda or
+hardware. Supplying `SONGPLUS_PANDA_PROFILE_JSON` to the ordinary wrapper/native
+entry fails closed rather than entering the old automatic reset/flash path.
+The four Python consumers use that variable only for a strict P0 synthetic
+profile. Invalid/unbound input cannot fall back to the official single-board
+policy. All profiles still deny real device access, CAN TX and firmware install.
+
+## Boundaries and message ownership
+
+The serialized owner captures `(registry generation, control epoch)` before
+reading/deserializing an event. Delayed old input cannot be assigned a fresh
+epoch. Configuration, fault recovery and disengagement retire control epochs,
+flush the routing queues, and require new enabled-state observations. Epoch is
+local metadata, not a cereal schema field or an authenticated security token.
+The native serializer and all consumers must use the same immutable profile.
+
+`pandaStates` always has two slots. A missing/stale/invalid slot invalidates the
+whole Event; unknown placeholders explicitly report unknown type and lost
+heartbeat. Available fault data can remain diagnostic but cannot make the Event
+valid. Valid output timestamps preserve the oldest required health/CAN-health
+observation, so republication cannot refresh an old snapshot. CAN and peripheral
+messages likewise retain their original receive/observation age.
+
+`CarParams.safetyConfigs` must contain exactly two explicit noOutput entries;
+parameters are per slot and alternativeExperience follows the unchanged shared
+CarParams field. No implicit ELM327, firmware query, OBD switch, allOutput or
+vehicle-specific safety selection is introduced. The noOutput gate permits only
+simulated dispatch in the fake backend; actual noOutput MCU safety forbids CAN TX.
+
+## Scheduler and resource policy
+
+The owner serializes callbacks, input admission and dispatch. Each `tick` issues
+at most one bounded control request per slot through P2, with a 5 ms cooperative
+budget per request. It checks freshness before issuing commands and validates
+command id/token/epoch/deadline again at completion. A failed or uncertain write
+retires that handle without replay. A blocked board therefore does not drain a
+queue or consume an unbounded retry loop ahead of its sibling. Hardware/kernel
+stall preemption is not claimed.
+
+| Item | Candidate offline policy |
+| --- | --- |
+| Health / CAN-health validity | age <250 ms, each board and each of its three buses |
+| Heartbeat | 100 ms schedule, completion age <250 ms |
+| SelfdriveState / sendcan | age <100 ms, original source timestamp |
+| P3 TX queue residence | <20 ms; max64 frames per slot |
+| DeviceState / fan demand | <750 ms, accommodating pinned 2 Hz producer |
+| Fan RPM observation | <250 ms; must be observed before simulated enable |
+| Camera demand when IR supported | <750 ms; unsupported IR produces no write |
+| Main control opportunity | candidate 10 ms; two control calls total <=10 ms if backends honor contract |
+| Fault exit | noOutput write, exact readback, disengaged heartbeat; three bounded opportunities |
+| Planned shutdown | three bounded exit rounds, then cancel handles/retire group |
+
+The reusable `PandadLoop` executes control work first, accepts at most16 captured
+ingress envelopes, then gives each board one CAN read/write opportunity. It
+schedules peripheral work at20Hz, pandaStates at10Hz and peripheralState at2Hz.
+The 10ms cycle budget is checked between cooperative operations; a budget overrun
+or cycle gap >=250ms closes the group and publishes invalid observations.
+Input/sink exceptions also close the group. No socket or physical device factory
+is provided in this synthetic-only stage.
+These fake-clock budgets are not C3XL timing measurements. Main-loop starvation
+fails closed on the next observation; abrupt process/power loss instead depends
+on the separately tested MCU heartbeat timeout. The original MCU watchdog does
+not run itself when its loop is stopped, and its fault is not immediate SILENT.
+
+## Peripheral and recovery policy
+
+Ignition is the OR of configured sources. A local DOS ignition=false cannot
+power down another live ignition source. Harness, power observations and fan/IR
+commands use their explicit roles and capabilities. A peripheral Event uses a
+single snapshot: fan RPM comes from the fan role and voltage/current from the
+power-monitor role, even when those roles belong to different boards. Its source
+time is the older of those observations; missing required values invalidate the
+whole unchanged-schema Event rather than inventing zero-valued sensors. No GPIO or power-save output
+is inferred from an unknown physical board. A missing/stale required fan sensor
+or deviceState observation closes the group; the code does not fabricate a safe
+physical fan output. Driver monitoring remains a separate unresolved hardware
+and vehicle requirement; unsupported IR is not permission to disable monitoring.
+
+A fresh transition to offroad immediately closes the control gate, flushes queued
+CAN and starts explicit disengagement. That accepted offroad observation is
+retained for a subsequent explicit configuration; continued enabled messages
+cannot keep heartbeat engaged while offroad. Enabled input also requires a fresh
+onroad deviceState.
+
+Recovery requires complete exact identities/new handles after a connection
+fault, a fresh offroad deviceState, explicit two-slot configuration and matching
+post-write health/CAN-health, fresh heartbeat and required peripheral readings,
+then a fresh disabled-to-enabled selfdriveState transition. Connection return
+alone never restores engagement. The real Python consumers remain disabled by
+P0 permissions even when synthetic messages are otherwise valid.
+
+## What this does not establish
+
+No MCU firmware build, C3XL execution, physical cooling behavior, operating-system
+change or vehicle safety validation is included. The default Linux SPI daemon is
+compiled and linked for regression, but only the explicit fake-I/O entry is run.
+The Python consumer tests execute selected actual functions/branches using real
+cereal bytes; they do not launch the full hardwared/card/selfdrived/UI processes.
+Real device discovery, profile binding, live Pub/Sub scheduling and deployment
+remain gated behind later hardware/safety/integration validation.
diff --git a/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/README.md b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/README.md
index 24b15c5..33e266e 100644
--- a/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/README.md
+++ b/openpilot/selfdrive/pandad/compatibility/README.md
@@ -120,3 +120,15 @@ runner `tools/validate_panda_sessions.py` replays all four patches and executes
 P0/P1/P2 regressions plus P3 on macOS/Linux. Existing active pandad/SPI sources
 remain unchanged. P4 must integrate health/safety, production lifecycle events,
 configuration/engagement barriers and message consumers before real use.
+
+## P4 integration (current stage)
+
+The earlier P0–P3 sections describe their historical standalone scope. P4 adds
+`ControlSession`, `PandadRuntime`, the bounded `PandadLoop`, unchanged-schema
+cereal adapters, an explicit `pandad --compat-offline` entry and opt-in Python
+consumer policy. See [P4-INTEGRATION.md](P4-INTEGRATION.md) and
+[CONTROL-SESSION.md](CONTROL-SESSION.md) for configuration/readback, liveness,
+source-age, role and re-engagement contracts. Every backend used by this entry
+is an in-memory fake; no physical profile can be activated. The Linux daemon is
+compiled and linked including its retained original SPI path, but only its
+explicit offline entry is executed. Real deployment permissions remain false.
